    {
      "id": "4ead1d74-100b-44d1-b341-11dc2ddae783",
      "name": "Extract invoice fields with AI",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "position": [
        4752,
        176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=You are an expert invoice data extraction specialist. Your task is to analyze any type of invoice document, including regular invoices, book invoices, and mixed-content files, and extract the required information with 100% accuracy. Follow these instructions exactly:\n\nEXTRACTION REQUIREMENTS:\nExtract the following fields from each invoice:\n\ncompany_name: Exact name of the company/business issuing the invoice\n\ninvoice_number: Unique invoice number (include all characters exactly as shown)\n\ninvoice_date: Date of issue format as in MM/DD/YYYY\n\nsales_tax: Sales tax amount as number only (if no sales tax, return \"N/A\")\n\nVAT_tax: VAT tax amount as number only (if no VAT, return \"N/A\")\n\ntotal_amount: Final total amount including all taxes (numbers only)\n\npaid_status: Payment status (Paid/Unpaid/Partial/Pending)\n\nterms: Payment terms (e.g., Net 30, Due on Receipt)\n\npdf_filename: PDF file name\n\npdf_url: Direct PDF file URL\n\ndrive_link: Google Drive or cloud storage link (if available)\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n\nIf any field is missing or unclear, return \"N/A\" for that field.\n\nsales_tax: If not explicitly mentioned, return \"N/A\" even if other taxes exist.\n\nVAT_tax: If not explicitly mentioned, return \"N/A\".\n\nAmounts: Remove all currency symbols, commas, and text — keep only plain numbers.\n\nDate: Preserve original date format exactly as found.\n\nCompany name: Match spelling exactly as in document.\n\nMultiple invoices in one file: Return an array of JSON objects — one per invoice.\n\nQUALITY ASSURANCE:\n\nDouble-check that sales_tax and VAT_tax are never included inside total_amount.\n\nValidate that extracted numbers exactly match the document.\n\nVerify that company names and invoice numbers are not altered or truncated.\n\nConfirm paid_status matches invoice wording exactly.\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n\nIf document is not an invoice, return:\n\n{\"error\": \"Not an invoice document\"}\n\n\nIf document is unreadable or corrupted, return:\n\n{\"error\": \"Document unreadable\"}\n\n\nIf invoice is a book invoice or non-business invoice, still extract all possible fields as per format.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nAlways return valid JSON:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"company_name\": \"extracted_company_name\",\n    \"invoice_number\": \"extracted_invoice_number\",\n    \"invoice_date\": \"extracted_date\",\n    \"sales_tax\": \"extracted_sales_tax_or_N/A\",\n    \"VAT_tax\": \"extracted_VAT_or_N/A\",\n    \"total_amount\": \"extracted_total_amount\",\n    \"paid_status\": \"extracted_status_or_N/A\",\n    \"terms\": \"extracted_terms_or_N/A\",\n    \"pdf_filename\": \"file_name.pdf\",\n    \"pdf_url\": \"document_url_or_N/A\",\n    \"drive_link\": \"cloud_link_or_N/A\"\n  }\n]\n\n\nIf there’s more than one invoice in a single PDF, add additional JSON objects to the array.\n",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=**Extracted File Content:**\n{{ $json.text }}\n**File Info:**\n- File Name: {{ $('Combine file and links').item.json.pdf_filename || $('Combine file and links').item.json.fileName }}\n- File Type: {{ $('Combine file and links').item.json.fileType }}\n- View URL: {{ $('Combine file and links').item.json.pdfUrl }}\n- Drive Folder: {{ $('Combine file and links').item.json.driveLink }}\n\n---"
        },
        "promptType": "define",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
